Subject: [PATCH 1/2] FEXCore: Let the code buffer grow to 512MB.

PACE License Services (LDSvc.exe, which iLok-protected plugins such as Neural DSP's talk to) has
92MB of x86-64 code. While it serves a plugin it needs more than 128MB of JIT code, so the
buffer filled every ~14 seconds, the whole cache was cleared and recompiled, and LDSvc used all
its time compiling: the plugin waited minutes for its license. With 512MB it clears once and
then goes idle.

The 128MB cap was there to keep branches short. Block linking already checks the range
(IsInt26) and falls back to an indirect jump, branches inside a block and to its jump thunks
stay within the block, and the dispatcher is reached through pointers in the CPU state. The
buffer is reserved, not committed, so programs that need less code use no more memory.
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/SharedCodeBufferManager.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/SharedCodeBufferManager.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/SharedCodeBufferManager.cpp
index eee502364..fa2dd71f2 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/SharedCodeBufferManager.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/SharedCodeBufferManager.cpp
@@ -13,8 +13,10 @@
 
 namespace FEXCore::CPU {
 static constexpr size_t INITIAL_CODE_SIZE = 1024 * 1024 * 16;
-// We don't want to move above 128MB atm because that means we will have to encode longer jumps
-static constexpr size_t MAX_CODE_SIZE = 1024 * 1024 * 128;
+// Pivuan: PACE's LDSvc (92 MB of x86 code) needs more than 128MB of JIT code; with 128MB it
+// clears the whole cache every few seconds and recompiles. Block linking already falls back to
+// indirect jumps past +-128MB, and branches inside a block stay short.
+static constexpr size_t MAX_CODE_SIZE = 1024 * 1024 * 512;
 
 CodeBuffer::CodeBuffer(size_t Size, bool ShouldBeNamed)
   : AllocatedSize(Size) {
